Claude Code asks once whether to use the project MCP server "lockssh"; approve it.
Optional: the calls below never touch data without the console's approval. To stop
Claude Code prompting for them, add them to "permissions.allow" in
.claude/settings.local.json (personal) or .claude/settings.json (shared):

  "mcp__lockssh__lockssh_status",
  "Bash(lockssh status:*)",
  "Bash(lockssh doctor:*)"

lockssh_run asks Claude Code each time: its allow-listed commands run on the host at once; other commands are decided on lockhub (lox approve, the lea deck or a paired phone).


